===Etymology 1===
{{PIE word|en|upó}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*Heh₃l-}}
Partly from the following:

* From {{inh|en|enm|sublimen}}, {{m|enm|sublime}}, {{m|enm|sublyme|t=to exalt, extol, glorify, honour; (''alchemy'') to refine (a substance) by vaporizing in a closed container; to obtain (a substance) by cooling vapour obtained through sublimation; to extract (a pure substance) from a mixture by sublimation; to sublimate (a substance)}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=sublīmen|pos=v|id=MED43560}}</ref> from {{der|en|frm|sublimer}}, {{der|en|fro|sublimer|t=to exalt, glorify, honour; to refine (a substance) by vaporizing in a closed container; of a substance: to undergo sublimation}} (modern {{cog|fr|sublimer}}), and from its {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|sublīmāre}}, the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|infinitive}} of {{m|la|sublimō|t=to elevate, raise; to soar}} (compare {{cog|LL.|sublimō|t=to elevate, raise; to exalt, glorify, honour; to sublimate, vaporize}}), from {{m|la|sublīmis|t=elevated, raised; exalted, uplifted, sublime; elevated in style}}<ref name="OED v">{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=1402234035|date=September 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref> (from {{m|la|sub-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘under; up to’}} + possibly ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*Heh₃l-|t=to bend}} (whence {{cog|la|līmen|t=threshold}} and {{m|la|līmus|t=askew; sideways}})) + {{m|la|-ō|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming regular first-{{glossary|conjugation}} {{glossary|verb}}s}}.
* From {{m|en|sublime|pos=adjective}}.<ref name="OED v"/>

